# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows offers "Checkout Windows-style, commit Unix-style" during install, which
# sets core.autocrlf=true. Under that setting every text file is checked out with CRLF —
# including the shell scripts this repository's CI toolchain is built from. bash then fails
# on the stray carriage return, typically as:
#
#     ./tool/ci/run-pipeline.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#     $'\r': command not found
#     Makefile:22: *** missing separator
#
# Those errors look like a broken script rather than what they are, a line-ending problem,
# and they cost an afternoon. `eol=lf` here makes the repository's intent override any
# local autocrlf setting, so a Windows checkout gets working scripts.

# --- must stay LF: interpreted by bash, make or python -------------------------
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
makefile        text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
.githooks/*     text eol=lf

# --- PowerShell: accepts either, but LF keeps diffs clean across platforms ------
*.ps1           text eol=lf
*.psm1          text eol=lf
*.psd1          text eol=lf

# --- Windows-native wrappers are conventionally CRLF ---------------------------
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# --- source, config and docs: LF everywhere ------------------------------------
# The JSON rule matters for CI, not just tidiness: the `web` job runs
# `npm run golden` and then fails if test-fixtures/golden-vectors.json differs
# from the committed file. Node writes "\n" on every platform, so pinning LF
# stops a CRLF checkout from making an unchanged golden vector look modified.
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.tsx           text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.jsx           text eol=lf
*.dart          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.gitignore     text eol=lf
*.gitattributes text eol=lf

# --- binary: never normalise ----------------------------------------------------
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.gz            binary
*.pyc           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.mp3           binary
*.wav           binary
*.opus          binary
